WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.900
It's Wednesday, November 18, and this is the Singularity Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.930
Here are the last 24 hours in superintelligence, in 3 minutes.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.570
Everyone wants in today.

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:20.940
Even Jensen Huang says he'd be honored to return as Nvidia's boss.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:23.110
He admits serious mistakes,

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:26.390
and the board reportedly has no plans to bring him back.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.190
Investors want in, too. Anthropic's stock market debut is so hot,

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:39.050
shares will likely cost more than planned.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:44.120
Sources told CNBC it'll likely top its range of $70 to $78.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.610
Trading should start Thursday.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.900
Meanwhile, Google DeepMind's drug spin-off,

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.790
Isomorphic Labs, just raised $5 billion.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:56.720
Its experimental drugs showed promise in the lab against cancer,

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:58.660
and they're heading for human trials.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.230
China wants in, too.

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:06.520
Reuters says Chinese firms are training their AI on answers from top American models.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.080
And NATO?

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:13.080
It's now using OpenAI's cyber-defense models to help protect allied networks.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.440
In Manila, Australia, India,

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:22.500
Japan and the US pledged over $85 million for trusted AI.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.040
Trump's take on AI? "Bigger than the industrial revolution.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:27.670
Bigger than the Internet."

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.030
Some good news.

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:36.670
A brain-tech startup called Science just raised $400 million for its eye implant.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.640
It's helping people whose sight is faili

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:41.840
ng with age read letters and words again.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.450
The catch? California's suing OpenAI,

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:51.420
whose agents went rogue in testing and hacked another firm.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:56.060
The state says OpenAI lost control of its agents more than 80 times.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.090
Robots want in, too.

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:07.700
Genesis AI just raised half a billion dollars to give them hands like ours.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:11.790
And Boston Dynamics' humanoid, Atlas,

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:15.780
will get its first tryout beyond carmakers, at a chip plant.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:20.360
Two of its robot dogs have already done over 90,000 inspections there.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:27.220
Everyone wants in. So let's make sure there's room for all of us.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.240
Zoom out, and the line only goes up.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.780
Somehow, the future keeps landing early.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.370
That's one day of news. Imagine what a year looks like.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.200
You've been watching the Singularity Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.120
Same time tomorrow?

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.010
Want the whole month? Hear more on November 27.
